--TEST--
`executeMany`'s one statement is a sink and its sets are not, so an untrusted value reaches every execution of a batch only through a placeholder — `rule:security/sink-predicate`, `rule:core-classes/db-one-api` and `rule:core-classes/db-statement-members`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The batch has one statement text and many sets, so `rule:security/sink-predicate`'s sink is
// per *batch* rather than per execution: a text assembled from outside would
// not be one bad query, it would be the same bad query run once per set.
tainted string $outside = "ada";

var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");

// The way through, and it is the whole point of the member: the untrusted
// value appears in every set and none of them can reach the text.
uint $written = $db->executeMany("insert into accounts (owner) values (?)", [
    [$outside],
    [$outside],
]);

// The refusal, at the one place a batch has a statement to put.
uint $refused = $db->executeMany($outside, [["ada"]]);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
   --> case.nvs:17:34
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
